From 09107b63b28006dccca47610e74358a8500e5c67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CHIBiNGA-1 <chibinga28@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:27:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Security review fixes: #1-#5
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five findings from a security review, each verified with a passing test:

#1 — Payment amount tampering (billing.py). submit_payment_request took
`amount` straight from the client with no check against the real price
of `plan_requested`. Now computed server-side from a fixed PLAN_PRICES
table; the client's amount field is accepted for backwards compatibility
but ignored. Verified end-to-end via a real TestClient request in
test_rate_limit.py::test_payment_request_amount_is_server_computed.

#2 — Non-constant-time admin key check (deps.py). require_admin compared
X-Admin-Key with plain `!=`, leaking timing info about how many leading
characters matched. Now uses hmac.compare_digest, consistent with the
WhatsApp webhook signature check elsewhere in the codebase.

#3 — WhatsApp link-code brute force (routers/whatsapp.py). The 6-digit
linking code had no attempt limiting. Added a 5-attempts/15-minute
lockout per sender number, with a distinct "too many attempts" reply.
Process-local (fine for the single Render instance this runs on).

#4 — No rate limiting anywhere in the API. Added slowapi: a 200/min-per-
IP app-wide default (main.py, app/limiter.py), plus tighter explicit
limits on the two most abuse-prone endpoints — payment-request
submission (5/hour) and WhatsApp link-code generation (10/hour).
Confirmed via slowapi's source that its middleware checks limits before
FastAPI resolves route dependencies, so this genuinely throttles admin-
key guessing too, not just successful requests — not just decorating
the admin endpoints themselves, which would run too late to matter.
Verified via test_rate_limit.py::test_payment_request_is_rate_limited,
a real TestClient request loop asserting the 6th call gets a 429.

#5 — AI-capture pipeline had no ceiling (shop_capture.py). A single
WhatsApp photo/text capture auto-filed straight into the ledger with no
human review, at any amount. Amounts over K5,000 (ZMW) now come back as
"needs_confirmation" instead of being auto-filed — held back for the
owner to add manually in the app if it's right. Applies to both the
sales-tally and supplier-note paths. Not a code bug fix so much as
capping the blast radius of trusting a single AI read of a photo/text;
see shop_capture.py's LARGE_AMOUNT_ZMW comment for the reasoning.

Testing notes: the existing direct-call test style in test_billing.py
bypasses the ASGI layer slowapi's middleware runs in, so those tests now
pass request=None and disable the limiter (limiter.enabled = False) —
the rate limit itself is verified for real, end-to-end, in the new
test_rate_limit.py via FastAPI's TestClient instead. Also required
StaticPool + check_same_thread=False on that file's SQLite test engine,
since TestClient runs the app in a separate thread and a plain
sqlite:///:memory: engine otherwise hands each thread its own empty
database.

requirements.txt: added slowapi==0.1.10.

All 68 backend tests pass (64 pre-existing + 4 new).
